name: Independent Signal Engine Builder

on:
  issue_comment:
    types: [created]

permissions:
  contents: write
  pull-requests: write
  issues: write

jobs:
  build:
    if: >-
      github.event.issue.pull_request == null &&
      github.actor == github.repository_owner &&
      contains(github.event.comment.body, '/opencode')
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 45

    steps:
      - name: Checkout repository
        uses: actions/checkout@v4
        with:
          ref: ${{ github.event.repository.default_branch }}
          fetch-depth: 0

      - name: Configure git
        run: |
          git config user.name "github-actions[bot]"
          git config user.email "41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com"

      - name: Build independent signal engine
        uses: anomalyco/opencode/github@latest
        env:
          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
        with:
          model: opencode/glm-5.3-flash-free
          agent: build
          use_github_token: true
          prompt: |
            You are the implementation agent for this repository only:
            rezajahanbakhsh2020-hue/independent-signal-engine.

            MISSION
            Build a standalone, reproducible Python signal research engine
            for XAUUSD, BTCUSDT and ETHUSDT. Work in small verifiable
            stages. Never claim a stage passed without executing it.

            STRICT BOUNDARIES
            - Modify this repository only.
            - Never access, modify, depend on, or publish to AI-Trading-Lab
              or AI-Trading-Lab-Platform.
            - Signal generation only. Never place orders, connect to brokers,
              or publish signals to external systems.
            - Never fabricate market data, test results, profitability,
              or completed work.
            - Do not merge pull requests automatically.
            - Inspect the repository first. If existing content conflicts
              with this mission, report the conflict; never delete or replace
              unrelated work.
            - Do not read or expose secrets.

            IMPLEMENTATION PLAN

            Stage 1: Foundations
            - Python 3.11+ project structure, dependency declarations,
              CLI, configuration, logging and README.
            - Canonical OHLCV schema with UTC-aware timestamps.
            - Validate ordering, duplicates, finite values, positive prices,
              nonnegative volume and OHLC candle geometry.
            - Detect stale data, missing intervals, insufficient history,
              and unfinished candles.
            - No silent repair, forward filling, synthetic candles, or
              cross-symbol/timeframe fallback.
            - Deterministic CSV input and reproducible offline tests.
            - Implement and test before proceeding.

            Stage 2: Strategies and backtesting
            - Implement SMA/EMA crossover, breakout momentum, trend pullback
              and mean-reversion strategies with explicit parameters.
            - Exclude the evaluation candle from breakout reference levels.
            - Prevent lookahead and future-data leakage.
            - Generate decisions only from eligible closed candles.
            - Backtest entry no earlier than the next bar's open.
            - Model configurable fees, spread and slippage.
            - Define conservative stop/target ambiguity handling.
            - Report trades, gross/net returns, drawdown, win rate,
              profit factor, exposure, turnover and exit reasons.
            - Define all metric formulas and zero-loss edge cases.

            Stage 3: Qualification and robustness
            - Chronological train/development, validation and untouched
              holdout partitions.
            - Walk-forward evaluation with documented purge/embargo rules.
            - Never tune on the final holdout or repeatedly reuse it to
              search for a winning strategy.
            - Configurable minimum evidence and risk gates; document that
              thresholds are policy choices, not guarantees.
            - Include costs, baseline comparison, fold consistency and
              cost-sensitivity checks.
            - If evidence is insufficient, return INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE.
            - If no strategy passes, return NO_QUALIFIED_STRATEGY.
            - Do not force a strategy to qualify.

            Stage 4: Signal interface and data adapters
            - Provide an offline evaluate mode using local CSV data.
            - Provide a signal mode only when a real, explicitly configured
              provider can supply sufficiently fresh data.
            - Add a public crypto OHLCV adapter if practical and testable.
            - Support gold data through an explicitly documented provider
              or CSV input; do not invent credentialless live gold data.
            - If data is unavailable or stale, return NO_TRADE with a clear
              reason or a controlled error. Never use stale cached data.
            - Output symbol, timeframe, BUY/SELL/NO_TRADE, strategy and
              version, UTC candle close, generation time, data quality,
              qualification state, reason codes and informational entry,
              stop-loss and take-profit references.
            - If no strategy qualifies, never emit BUY or SELL.
            - No orders, broker integration or external signal publication.

            INITIAL COVERAGE
            Target XAUUSD, BTCUSDT and ETHUSDT on 5m, 15m, 1h, 4h and 1d.
            Keep symbol and timeframe datasets strictly independent.
            Do not pretend every combination has sufficient data or qualifies.

            TESTING AND EVIDENCE
            - Add meaningful unit and integration tests for validation,
              indicators, strategies, leakage, costs, qualification and CLI.
            - Keep core tests network-independent.
            - Run the actual test suite and offline smoke tests.
            - Test stale-data rejection and a no-qualified-strategy case.
            - Verify that no order execution or external publishing exists.
            - Fix genuine failures; never weaken tests merely to pass.
            - Report exact commands, test counts and outcomes.
            - If time or context limits prevent completion, stop safely and
              report completed stages, incomplete stages and blockers.
            - Do not report an unimplemented feature as complete.

            DELIVERABLES
            Maintain a clear README covering setup, commands, data formats,
            strategy parameters, metric definitions, assumptions, validation,
            limitations and reproducibility.
            Make focused changes, preserve useful existing work, and provide
            an evidence-based completion report.
